---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
  name: 'Vemor',
  description: 'AI automation and managed operations for small businesses. Built and run by a 14-year industry operator. Bilingual, English and Spanish.',
  url: 'https://vemor.ai',
  priceRange: '$$',
  areaServed: ['San Diego', 'Southern California', 'United States', 'Mexico'],
};
---
<Base
  title="Vemor | AI Automation Built by Someone Who's Done Your Job"
  description="AI automation and managed operations for small businesses. Phones answered, books reconciled, busywork gone. Built and run by a 14-year industry operator. English y español."
  schema={schema}
  path="/"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="hero-tagline">AI Automation &amp; Managed Operations</span>
    <h1>AI automation built by someone <span class="gold">who's done your job.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      I spent 14 years running shops, writing estimates, and adjusting claims before I ever
      wrote a line of code. Now I build the systems that kill your busywork, and I run them
      for you. In English y en español.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Let's talk about what's eating your time</a>
      <a href="/voice" class="btn-secondary">Hear the AI receptionist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-proof">
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">14+</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Years inside the industries I automate</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">1,000+</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Shop visits as an adjuster</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">EN / ES</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Bilingual, natively</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">24/7</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Systems that run while you sleep</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STORY (CSC land-and-expand) -->
  <div class="section-full soft" id="results">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">Real Work, Real Client</span>
      <h2 class="title">It started with one report. It became four systems.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        A four-location smog inspection operation in San Diego's South Bay. This is how
        Vemor engagements actually go: one problem solved, then the next one.
      </p>
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="story-stats">
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">2+ hrs/day</div>
              <div class="stat-label">of manual reconciliation, eliminated</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">Same day</div>
              <div class="stat-label">payment errors caught, not weeks later</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">4 systems</div>
              <div class="stat-label">live: reporting, RFID tracking, AI phones, security</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">Month 1</div>
              <div class="stat-label">"The system paid for itself"</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>Where it started</h4>
          <p>
            Every night, someone had to manually reconcile sales across four stations.
            Compare printouts, hunt for voided invoices, check discounts, find payment
            errors. Two-plus hours a day, and mistakes still slipped through for weeks.
          </p>
          <h4>What we built</h4>
          <p>
            An automated pipeline that reads their existing point-of-sale database every
            night, reconciles everything, flags exceptions, and emails a clean report
            before opening. No new software to learn. No data migration. It sits on top
            of what they already had.
          </p>
          <h4>What happened next</h4>
          <p>
            Trust earned, the next problem came up: rental equipment going missing.
            We built RFID tracking across all four locations. Then a bilingual AI agent
            for the phones. Then security management. One relationship, four systems,
            all running today as a managed service.
          </p>
          <div class="pull-quote">"The system paid for itself in the first month."</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT WE DO -->
  <section id="services">
    <span class="label">What We Do</span>
    <h2 class="title">Two ways to work with Vemor.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Start small with your phones, or hand off your operations. Every client is different, so every build is different. What's the same: you get the finished result, not a tool you have to figure out.</p>
    <div class="cards-2">
      <div class="card featured">
        <span class="card-badge">The Core Service</span>
        <h3>Managed AI Operations</h3>
        <p class="tagline">Your operations, handled end to end.</p>
        <p>
          I find the busywork eating your week, build the automation that kills it, and
          then I run it. Reconciliation, reporting, outreach, databases, custom tools.
          You get a builder and an operator, not a consultant with a slide deck.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Audit, architect, build, operate, expand</li>
          <li>Built on top of the tools you already use</li>
          <li>Ongoing monitoring and weekly reporting</li>
          <li>Nothing locks you in. Ever.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/operations" class="card-cta">How it works →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-badge">Start Here</span>
        <h3>VemorVoice</h3>
        <p class="tagline">Your phones answered. 24/7. Both languages.</p>
        <p>
          A bilingual AI receptionist that answers every call, books appointments,
          handles FAQs, and hands off to you when it matters. Set up in days.
          Cancel by unforwarding your number.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>English and Spanish, mid-call, natively</li>
          <li>Books straight into your calendar</li>
          <li>Weekly report of every call and booking</li>
          <li>Flat monthly rate, no per-minute games</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/voice" class="card-cta">Hear it live →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">The Process</span>
      <h2 class="title">Five steps. No mystery.</h2>
      <p class="sub">This is the same process behind every system Vemor runs today.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <h3>Audit</h3>
          <p>We map where your time actually goes and find the automation worth doing first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <h3>Architect</h3>
          <p>Design the system around your existing tools. Build what's needed, buy what's smarter, skip the rest.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <h3>Build</h3>
          <p>I build it myself. Automations, AI agents, databases, integrations, hardware if the job calls for it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <h3>Operate</h3>
          <p>I run it. Monitoring, maintenance, reports. You don't need an IT department.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">5</div>
          <h3>Expand</h3>
          <p>When the next thing hurts, we automate that too. Trust first, always.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHY TRUST -->
  <section>
    <span class="label">Why Owners Trust This</span>
    <h2 class="title">If I disappeared tomorrow, your business wouldn't notice.</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        That's not modesty, that's the design. Everything Vemor builds sits <strong>on top of
        what you already have</strong>. Your point-of-sale stays your point-of-sale. Your data stays
        yours. Forward your phone line to the AI agent; unforward it and you're back where
        you started. No platform migrations, no contracts that trap you, no system only I
        can operate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most AI agencies learned your industry from a sales call. I managed smog stations
        for six years, wrote collision estimates, and spent eight years walking into shops
        as a field adjuster. When I automate a workflow, it's because <strong>I've personally done
        that workflow</strong> and I know exactly which parts deserve to die.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NORTH STAR -->
  <div class="section-full soft north-star">
    <p class="north-star-text">"Vemor exists because <em>life's too short</em> to spend it on busywork."</p>
  </div>

  <!-- FINAL CTA -->
  <section style="text-align:center;">
    <h2 class="title">Ready to get your time back?</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
      Twenty minutes, no pitch deck. Tell me what's eating your week and I'll tell you
      honestly whether it's worth automating.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Call</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
